}},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" 13194139534529 true] [17592186293372 1113 #uuid "ccc82d1a-8b77-5855-b94b-af517ea6204a" 13194139534529 true] [17592186293372 1145 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{2}^{n+4}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{4}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{n}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =16{(\\frac{2}{x})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{2}{x}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge 2.\n$$" 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293374 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293375 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293376 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293377 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293378 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1041 "selection" 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293378 13194139534529 true] [17592186293373 1110 #uuid "52b8db26-97d0-5544-b6e5-d7e0671f2706" 13194139534529 true] [17592186293374 1034 "x>2" 13194139534529 true] [17592186293374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534529 true] [17592186293374 1111 #uuid "f47ee072-c12d-